From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sample_rsa: initialize EVP output buffer lengths

EVP_PKEY_encrypt() and EVP_PKEY_decrypt() require the caller to pass the
available output-buffer size through the output-length argument.  Passing
uninitialized stack values makes the sample fail with RSA_R_BAD_LENGTH on
OpenSSL 3.

Initialize both lengths from their destination buffers.  Leave one byte in
the plaintext buffer for the terminating NUL added after decryption.
---
 sample_crypto/sample_rsa/sample_rsa.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sample_crypto/sample_rsa/sample_rsa.c b/sample_crypto/sample_rsa/sample_rsa.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/sample_crypto/sample_rsa/sample_rsa.c
+++ b/sample_crypto/sample_rsa/sample_rsa.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 	// 可选：显式设置填充（默认是 PKCS#1 v1.5）
 	// EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_rsa_padding(enc_ctx, RSA_PKCS1_OAEP_PADDING);
 
-	size_t outlen;
+	size_t outlen = sizeof(ciphertext);
 	if (EVP_PKEY_encrypt(enc_ctx, ciphertext, &outlen, plaintext, strlen((char *)plaintext)) <= 0) {
 		handleErrors("EVP_PKEY_encrypt Failed");
 	}
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 	// 填充必须与加密一致（默认 PKCS#1 v1.5）
 	// EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_rsa_padding(dec_ctx, RSA_PKCS1_OAEP_PADDING);
 
-	size_t decrypted_len;
+	size_t decrypted_len = sizeof(decryptedtext) - 1;
 	if (EVP_PKEY_decrypt(dec_ctx, decryptedtext, &decrypted_len, ciphertext, ciphertext_len) <= 0) {
 		handleErrors("EVP_PKEY_decrypt Failed");
 	}
-- 
